					<description><![CDATA[Today’s headlines: Supreme Court, Gibo Teodoro, Alex Eala]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p>Here are today&#8217;s headlines – the latest news in the Philippines and around the world:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://www.rappler.com/philippines/chief-justice-candidates-jbc-shortlist-october-2026/"><strong>All 5 chief justice candidates make it to JBC shortlist</strong></a><strong>  </strong></li>
</ul>



<p>All five Supreme Court associate justices aspiring to become the country’s next chief justice make it to the Judicial and Bar Council’s shortlist.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/inside-track/gibo-teodoro-china-defense-attache-asean-meeting-cebu/"><strong>Gibo snubs China at ADMM-Plus</strong></a><strong> </strong></li>
</ul>



<p>Philippines Defense Secretary Gibo Teodoro snubs the welcoming event of China’s defense attaché to Manila Senior Captain Yang Lei.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://www.rappler.com/philippines/department-agriculture-weak-peso-push-up-imported-rice-fertilizer-prices/"><strong>DA: Weak peso to push up imported rice, fertilizer prices</strong></a><strong> </strong></li>
</ul>



<p>Department of Agriculture spokesman Arnel de Mesa says the weakening peso will push up prices of imports such as rice, fertilizer, and other farm goods.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://www.rappler.com/world/middle-east/netanyahu-caretaker-inconclusive-israeli-election/"><strong>Netanyahu set to remain caretaker after inconclusive Israeli election</strong></a></li>
</ul>



<p>Benjamin Netanyahu will likely remain as Israel’s caretaker prime minister after unexpectedly strong backing among Jewish voters.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://www.rappler.com/people/athletes/alex-eala-talia-gibson-tennis-toray-pan-pacific-open-october-28-2026/"><strong>Alex Eala advances to Toray Pan Pacific quarterfinals after besting Talia Gibson</strong></a></li>
</ul>



<p>Filipina tennis star Alex Eala pulled off a thrilling win over Australia’s Talia Gibson, 4-6, 6-2, 6-0, in the Toray Pan Pacific Open round of 16 match in Tokyo, Japan, on Wednesday, October 28. <strong>– Rappler.com</strong></p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
