		<item>
		<title>ECB President Lagarde resigns at time of mounting challenges for Europe</title>
		<link>https://www.rappler.com/business/ecb-president-christine-lagarde-resigns-october-2026/</link>
					<comments>https://www.rappler.com/business/ecb-president-christine-lagarde-resigns-october-2026/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Reuters]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:13:44 +0800</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Business]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Europe]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[World]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[European Union]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[France]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false"></guid>

					<description><![CDATA[A source with direct knowledge of the matter says Christine Lagarde resigned so she could weigh in on political matters in her native France and globally]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p>FRANKFURT, Germany – European Central Bank President Christine Lagarde announced her resignation on Thursday, October 29, ending months of speculation about her future just as <a href="https://www.rappler.com/topic/european-union/">Europe</a> enters a period of rising economic volatility and divisive electoral politics.</p>



<p>Lagarde will step down on February 7, giving current European Union leaders time to pick a successor well before a French presidential election that polls show far-right candidate Marine Le Pen is favored to win.</p>



<p>The move comes as the ECB battles inflation risks from an Iran-driven oil shock while a sharp rise in bond yields, especially in <a href="https://www.rappler.com/topic/france">France</a>, threatens to dampen growth.</p>



<p>&#8220;I leave this institution with a sense of good work done and an ECB that is fit for the future,&#8221; Lagarde said in a short video shared on social media.</p>



<p>A source with direct knowledge of the matter said Lagarde had resigned so she could weigh in on political matters in her native France and globally. As ECB president, she was expected to remain neutral to safeguard the institution&#8217;s independence.</p>



<p>European Council President Antonio Costa said in a statement the process to find a successor for Lagarde would begin immediately. The former central bank governors of the Netherlands and Spain, Klaas Knot and Pablo Hernandez de Cos, are widely seen as frontrunners.</p>



<p>&#8220;The rumored successors are both very competent, well-established central bankers, so for markets, it won’t matter too much,&#8221; Piet Haines Christiansen, an economist at Danske Bank, said.</p>



<p>Financial markets did not move much after the announcement, with some analysts noting the ECB had by now built a reputation that outlived any of its leaders.</p>



<p>&#8220;The ECB is now quite well-established, the market is familiar with the way it operates,&#8221; Goldman Sachs&#8217; head of Fixed Income Macro Investing Simon Dangoor said. &#8220;Our view is that institutional behavior is likely to outlast Lagarde, and be quite similar, whoever takes over.&#8221;</p>



<p>Lagarde&#8217;s term was scheduled to run until the end of October 2027, but speculation about an early departure had been mounting for months, with the World Economic Forum seen as a likely destination.</p>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-rate-hikes-and-bond-turmoil">Rate hikes and bond turmoil</h5>



<p>The ECB is in the middle of a rate-hiking cycle aimed at preventing an oil-price shock linked to the Iran war from feeding into other prices and wages.</p>



<p>But it must also contend with a surge in government bond yields — especially in debt-laden France — that has pushed up borrowing costs for households and businesses and which Lagarde has said will curb growth and inflation.</p>



<p>Caught between persistent inflation fueled by a renewed surge in energy costs and deteriorating financing conditions, the ECB is widely expected to keep its deposit rate at 2.5% on Thursday while signaling that another increase, potentially as soon as December, remains likely.</p>



<p>&#8220;There is likely a low bar to another hike in December, given the likelihood of another upward revision of the ECB&#8217;s inflation forecast due to higher energy prices,&#8221; Oliver Rakau at Oxford Economics said.</p>



<p>The ECB is due to announce its interest rate decision at 1315 GMT on Thursday, followed by Lagarde&#8217;s regular press conference at 1345 GMT.</p>



<p>Money markets are currently pricing another three rate increases from the ECB by the end of next year, which would take the deposit rate to 3.25%, a level that is widely seen as restricting economic growth.</p>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-french-turmoil-in-focus-but-no-action">French turmoil in focus but no action</h5>



<p>The more immediate challenge for policymakers may be turmoil in bond markets.</p>



<p>A global rise in yields, fueled by stronger growth expectations, higher debt issuance and massive investment linked to artificial intelligence, is pushing up borrowing costs for governments, households and businesses alike.</p>



<p>In France, investors have become increasingly uneasy about the country&#8217;s growing debt burden and uncertain fiscal outlook following this year&#8217;s elections. Concerns have been amplified by suggestions from parts of the political left that debt held by the ECB could be written off.</p>



<p>The result has been a sharp increase in French borrowing costs. France is now paying some of the highest yields in a quarter-century to raise money on bond markets, while the premium investors demand to hold French debt over benchmark German bonds is larger than for any other euro zone country.</p>



<p>That has fueled speculation that the ECB might be forced to respond, if only verbally for now.</p>



<p>&#8220;They&#8217;ve typically come up with a new tool that&#8217;s customised for that specific set of circumstances,&#8221; said Dangoor at Goldman Sachs.</p>



<p>The ECB&#8217;s first line of defence would probably be flexible reinvestment of proceeds from bonds acquired during its vast asset-purchase programs of the previous decade.</p>



<p>Beyond that, it could activate its never-used Transmission Protection Instrument, a scheme designed to counter what policymakers deem unjustified market pressure. – <strong>Rappler.com</strong></p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.rappler.com/business/ecb-president-christine-lagarde-resigns-october-2026/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
		
<image>https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/ecb-christine-lagarde-february-5-2026-reuters.jpg</image>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>FACT CHECK: No report of Indonesian President confronting, scolding Marcos</title>
		<link>https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/fact-check/no-report-indonesian-president-confronting-scolding-ferdinand-marcos-jr/</link>
					<comments>https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/fact-check/no-report-indonesian-president-confronting-scolding-ferdinand-marcos-jr/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Rappler.com]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:07:04 +0800</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Fact Check]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Newsbreak]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Philippine News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ferdinand Marcos Jr.]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Indonesia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Marcos Fact Checks]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false"></guid>

					<description><![CDATA[The video contains no footage, audio, or documentation of the alleged confrontation. Instead, the content features an unidentified male commentator reacting to a third-party social media post unrelated to the claim.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p><strong>Claim:</strong> Indonesia’s president publicly confronted and scolded President Ferdinand Marcos Jr., telling him to &#8220;fix yourself and your country.&#8221;</p>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-rating-false"><strong>Rating:</strong> FALSE</h5>



<p><strong>Why we fact-checked this:</strong> The YouTube channel &#8220;PINAS BALITA TV&#8221; with 175,000 subscribers published a video bearing the title: <em>&#8220;GRABE NA! NAKAKAH1YA TO! IND0NESIAN PRESIDENT HARAPANG SINUP4L-P4L at NA-REALTALK si BEBE EM?&#8221;</em> (This is too much! How embarrassing! Indonesian President confronted and engaged BBM in real talk?)</p>



<p>The video’s thumbnail, posted on October 17, 2026, shows an enraged Indonesian President Prabowo Subianto pointing directly at the President&#8217;s face before press microphones and cameras. </p>



<p>In the video&#8217;s original thumbnail, the uploader claimed that the Indonesian leader told Marcos to <em>“</em>fix your country and yourself,<em>”</em> though this line has since been edited out as of writing.<br><br>As of writing, the video has garnered 3,100 views and 234 likes.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" width="817" height="1024" decoding="async" src="https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/fact-check-full-post-indonesian-president-scolding-marcos.jpg?fit=1024%2C1024" alt="" class="wp-image-3258074" srcset="https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/fact-check-full-post-indonesian-president-scolding-marcos.jpg?fit=817%2C1024&amp;zoom=1 817w, https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/fact-check-full-post-indonesian-president-scolding-marcos.jpg?fit=817%2C1024&amp;zoom=0.5 409w, https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/fact-check-full-post-indonesian-president-scolding-marcos.jpg?fit=817%2C1024&amp;zoom=0.25 204w" sizes="(max-width: 817px) 100vw, 817px" /></figure>



<p><strong>The facts:</strong> No credible news reports or official footage confirm that Indonesia’s Subianto confronted or publicly engaged Marcos in real talk before the press.<br><br>AI image detectors <a href="https://isthisai.com/scan/8c1102a3-8cbc-4f4f-9327-2f63d640006f" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">IsThisAI</a> reveal that the thumbnail of the video is 99% likely to be AI-generated. Meanwhile, <a href="https://sightengine.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">SightEngine</a> flagged it as 87% likely to have used generative AI, and <a href="https://truthscan.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">TruthScan</a> estimated an 85% edit probability with high confidence.<br><br>“The background crowd appears to be cloned or manipulated, showing unnatural repetition patterns. Shadows on the subjects&#8217; faces and clothing are inconsistent, further suggesting digital editing,” the TruthScan findings said.</p>



<p><strong>Lack of evidence: </strong>The video contains no footage, audio, or documentation of any confrontation. Instead, the content features an unidentified male commentator reacting to a third-party social media post.</p>



<p>The commentator compares how both governments address climate challenges — particularly <a href="https://www.pna.gov.ph/article/pbbm-serious-in-el-nino-response-palace-says-amid-balde-remarks-criticism" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">El Niño</a> — contrasting Indonesia&#8217;s reported distribution of water pumps with the Philippine government&#8217;s recommendation to <a href="https://www.pna.gov.ph/article/pbbm-serious-in-el-nino-response-palace-says-amid-balde-remarks-criticism">collect rainwater using buckets</a>. The commentator heavily criticized the administration’s suggested solution.<em><br><br></em><strong>Existing ties: </strong>Diplomatic ties between the Philippines and Indonesia remain stable as of writing. Both countries held <a href="https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/ph-indonesia-agree-to-work-together-to-tackle-regional-challenges-pbbm/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">bilateral meetings</a> in 2024, and Marcos, along with First Lady Liza Araneta Marcos, formally <a href="https://youtu.be/zGjmwbXEjVU?si=ykxWmOp-N58qvQlw" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">welcomed</a> President Subianto during the opening ceremony of the 48th ASEAN Summit held in Cebu in May 2026.</p>



<p>Marcos also traveled to Jakarta to attend Subianto&#8217;s presidential inauguration in 2024.</p>



<p><strong>Debunked:</strong> Marcos has been a frequent subject of <a href="https://www.rappler.com/topic/marcos-fact-checks/">false claims</a>, particularly controversies:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/fact-check/no-official-statement-ferdinand-marcos-jr-intent-declare-war/">FACT CHECK: No official statement implies Marcos’ intent to declare war, martial law</a></li>



<li><a href="https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/fact-check/marcos-statement-cancel-2028-election-false-context/">FACT CHECK: Marcos statement claiming to cancel 2028 election is taken out of context</a></li>



<li><a href="https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/fact-check/marcos-fake-quote-protecting-sara-duterte-corruption/">FACT CHECK: Marcos Jr. did not say protecting VP Duterte from her case is ‘corruption’</a></li>



<li><a href="https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/fact-check/marcos-fake-quote-six-year-extension-presidential-term/">FACT CHECK: Marcos did not say he wants another 6-year presidential term</a></li>
</ul>



<p>&nbsp;<strong>&#8211; Lyndee Buenagua/Rappler.com</strong></p>



<p><em>Lyndee Buenagua is a Metro Manila-based journalist who primarily covers Bicol and Baguio. She is also an alumna of </em><a href="https://www.rappler.com/philippines/journalism-nation-building-foundation-awards-aries-rufo-factsmatterph-fellowships-2024/"><em>Aries Rufo Journalism Fellowship</em></a><em> of Rappler for 2024.</em></p>



<p>Keep us aware of suspicious Facebook pages, groups, accounts, websites, articles, or photos in your network by contacting us at factcheck@rappler.com. Let us battle disinformation one <a href="https://rappler.com/newsbreak/fact-check">Fact Check</a> at a time.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/fact-check/no-report-indonesian-president-confronting-scolding-ferdinand-marcos-jr/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
		
		<media:thumbnail url="https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/fact-check-full-post-indonesian-president-scolding-marcos.jpg?resize=75%2C75&amp;crop_strategy=attention" />
		<media:content url="https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/fact-check-full-post-indonesian-president-scolding-marcos.jpg" medium="image">
			<media:title type="html">fact-check-full-post-indonesian-president-scolding-marcos</media:title>
			<media:thumbnail url="https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/fact-check-full-post-indonesian-president-scolding-marcos.jpg?resize=75%2C75&amp;crop_strategy=attention" />
		</media:content>
<image>https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/fact-check-carousel-indonesian-president-scolding-marcos.jpg</image>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>LIST: Evidence submitted by prosecution to impeach court vs Sara Duterte</title>
		<link>https://www.rappler.com/philippines/list-evidence-submitted-prosecution-impeachment-court-sara-duterte/</link>
					<comments>https://www.rappler.com/philippines/list-evidence-submitted-prosecution-impeachment-court-sara-duterte/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Dwight de Leon]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:12:15 +0800</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[National News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Newsbreak]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Philippine News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Rappler IQ]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Anti-Money Laundering Council]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Bureau of Internal Revenue]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[House of Representatives]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Office of the Ombudsman]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Philippine National Police]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Sara Duterte]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Sara Duterte impeachment]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC)]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Senate of the Philippines]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false"></guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Rappler obtained a copy of the prosecution's formal offer of evidence. Here are key documents that are part of the submission.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="has-drop-cap">After the prosecution wrapped up the presentation of its case in the impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Duterte, it submitted its formal offer of evidence to the court. </p>



<p>It&#8217;s a mandatory submission that allows the prosecution to state the specific purpose of each piece of evidence, although the defense may still contest it.</p>



<p>Rappler obtained a copy of the formal offer of evidence. Below are key documents that are part of the submission.</p>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-1-her-statements-of-assets-liabilities-and-net-worth-salns-from-2007-to-2025-from-the-office-of-the-ombudsman">1. Her Statements of Assets, Liabilities, and Net Worth (SALNs) from 2007 to 2025, from the Office of the Ombudsman</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Her SALNs show her or her husband&#8217;s continued stake with Gencorp, Metro City Chow Foods Corporation, and Cale88 Foods Corporation, while she is already a sitting vice president, apparently in violation of Article VII, Section 13 of the Constitution.</li>



<li>Her SALNs supposedly prove she did not declare her 51 firearms, her properties in Matina and Kembali, her cash on hand and in bank from 2019 to 2025, and various insurance policies and investments.</li>



<li>Prosecutors say her ending bank balances from 2022 to 2025 do not match her declared total personal assets for those years.</li>
</ul>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-2-corporate-records-of-companies-tied-to-her-and-her-husband-mans-carpio">2. Corporate records of companies tied to her and her husband Mans Carpio</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>The prosecutors submitted SEC records of the following entities to prove that she and/or her husband are either an incorporator, shareholder, or member of the board of directors.
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>City Hall King Chow Foods Corporation</li>



<li>Metro City Chow Foods Corporation</li>



<li>Gencorp Industries</li>



<li>Cale88 Foods Corporation</li>



<li>Mati City Ice Plant and Cold Storage</li>



<li>Geometry Security and Investigation Agency</li>



<li>Great Jolly Times Food Corp</li>



<li>Timesquare Bee Foods Corp</li>



<li>Davao New Royal Taipan Foods Corporation</li>



<li>Davao Emerging Taipans Corporation</li>



<li>3Kids Trucking Services</li>



<li>CYK&amp;T Davao Corporation</li>



<li>SGT Fortune Horse Corporation</li>



<li>Davao Bounty Times Foods Corporation</li>



<li>Madayaw Fisheries</li>



<li>Amianan Shores</li>



<li>Cabletow 88 Shipping and Marine Services</li>



<li>Carpio Lawyers</li>



<li>Pikimong Pikimong Philippines Corporation</li>



<li>JTC Group of Companies Philippines</li>
</ul>
</li>



<li>The general information sheets and/or audited financial statements of many of these companies supposedly prove Duterte and/or her husband did not receive dividend income from the firms.</li>



<li>The SEC records of some of these companies also show that Duterte and/or her husband subscribed a paid-up capital to the firms, yet the shareholdings were not declared in the SALN.</li>
</ul>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-3-philippine-statistics-authority-records">3. Philippine Statistics Authority records</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Their marriage certificate establishes that there is no prenuptial agreement between them.</li>
</ul>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-4-philippine-government-electronic-procurement-system-philggeps-records-of-contracts-won-by-their-supposed-companies">4. Philippine Government Electronic Procurement System (PhilgGEPS) records of contracts won by their supposed companies</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>The procurement records between Gencorp and either Davao City LGU, PhilHealth Region 10, and the Overseas Workers Welfre Administration Region 11 supposedly prove she violated the constitutional prohibition on government officials being financially interested in government contracts.
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Most notably, Gencorp <a href="https://www.rappler.com/philippines/more-gencorp-contracts-davao-city-hall-confirmed-impeachment-trial-september-22-2026/">bagged 19 contracts</a> worth at least P34 million with the Davao City LGU led by her brother Mayor Sebastian Duterte from 2022 to 2026.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>


	<div class="shortcode shortcode--youtube">
		<div class="youtube-video" data-youtube-id="CcQSyB4t6mM" data-title="">
	<button class="youtube-video__load-button">
				<span class="screen-reader-text">Play  Video</span>
	</button>
	<img
	src="https://img.youtube.com/vi/CcQSyB4t6mM/hqdefault.jpg"
	data-srcset="https://img.youtube.com/vi/CcQSyB4t6mM/default.jpg 120w, https://img.youtube.com/vi/CcQSyB4t6mM/mqdefault.jpg 320w, https://img.youtube.com/vi/CcQSyB4t6mM/hqdefault.jpg 480w, https://img.youtube.com/vi/CcQSyB4t6mM/sddefault.jpg 640w"
	data-sizes=""
	data-src="https://img.youtube.com/vi/CcQSyB4t6mM/hqdefault.jpg"
	class="youtube-video__image-overlay"
	alt="LIST: Evidence submitted by prosecution to impeach court vs Sara Duterte"
	loading="lazy"
>
	<div class="youtube-video__iframe"></div>
</div>
	</div>
	


<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-5-records-of-her-firearms-with-the-philippine-national-police">5. Records of her firearms with the Philippine National Police</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>The certifications issued by the PNP Firearms and Explosives Office (FEO) to Duterte and her husband document their combined total of 51 guns worth P7.2 million, assets not declared in her SALN.</li>
</ul>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-6-land-registration-authority-lra-records-of-relevant-properties">6. Land Registration Authority (LRA) records of relevant properties</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>The transfer certificates of title, among other LRA documents, detail Duterte and her husband&#8217;s properties in Kembali and Matina, which are absent from her SALNs.</li>
</ul>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-7-anti-money-laundering-council-amlc-reports">7. Anti-Money Laundering Council (AMLC) reports</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>AMLC records detail covered transaction reports (CTRs) and suspicious transaction reports (STRs) involving Duterte and her husband worth P4.4 billion from 2007 to 2025.
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>The amount includes P424 million during her stint as vice president.</li>
</ul>
</li>



<li>.The AMLC reports cover large US dollar cash withdrawals, time deposit renewals, single-day multi-million peso transfers, and significant over-the-counter cash withdrawals/check encashments.</li>



<li>One of their companies, Cale88, supposedly received P368.8 million in foreign remittances, including P319.3 million from senders in China.</li>
</ul>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-8-bank-records">8. Bank records</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Prosecutors submitted records from the following banks:
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>BDO Unibank (seven accounts)</li>



<li>BPI (six accounts)</li>



<li>Landbank (one account)</li>



<li>Metrobank (three accounts)</li>



<li>Philippine Savings Bank (two accounts)</li>



<li>Security Bank (one account)</li>



<li>PNB (four accounts)</li>



<li>Unionbank (one account)</li>



<li>Asia United Bank (two accounts)</li>
</ul>
</li>



<li>Prosecutors say the 27 bank accounts show total year-end balances of P207.6 million from 2022 to 2025, which were not declared in her SALNs for those years.</li>
</ul>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-9-insurance-and-investment-company-records">9. Insurance and investment company records</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Duterte and her husband have active insurance policies across seven companies from 2022 to 2025, none of which were declared in her SALN.</li>



<li>These companies are:
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>BDO Life (two insurance investments)</li>



<li>BDO Securities (seven securities/ other investments)</li>



<li>BPI AIA<strong> </strong>(one insurance investment)</li>



<li>FWD Life (one insurance investment)</li>



<li>Manulife (six insurance investments)</li>



<li>Allianz (two insurance investments)</li>



<li>Prulife<strong> </strong>(five insurance investments)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-10-tax-records-with-the-bureau-and-internal-revenue-bir">10. Tax records with the Bureau and Internal Revenue (BIR)</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>The BIR records of the couple show their combined income of P85.3 million from 2027 to 2025, which prosecutors assert is vastly disproportionate to their declared net worth and calculated unexplained wealth.</li>



<li>Some of the documents also show that Duterte earned income from practicing law and received funds from Davao City Hall while she is vice president.</li>
</ul>



<h5 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-11-forensic-examination-report">11. Forensic examination report</h5>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>The forensic report of veteran Certified Public Accountant or CPA lawyer Alexander Cabrera found that Duterte and her husband have an unexplained wealth of at least P817.8 million from 2022 to 2025.</li>
</ul>


