					 	</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

<div class="related-article ">
			<div class="related-article__container">
				<div class="related-article__text">
					<div class="related-article__eyebrow">Must Read</div>
					<div class="related-article__title">
						<a class="related-article__title-link" href="https://www.rappler.com/philippines/supreme-court-associate-justice-candidates-marcos-pick-2026-part-2/">
							<h1 class="related-article__title-text"> Part 2: Old-timer bets in the running to be Marcos&#8217; 2nd SC justice </h1>
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="related-article__media-container">
					<div class="related-article__media">
						<a href="https://www.rappler.com/philippines/supreme-court-associate-justice-candidates-marcos-pick-2026-part-2/">
					 		<img decoding="async" width="449" height="253" src="https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/SJ-CANDIDATES-02.jpg?fit=449%2C449" class=" wp-image-3255160 wp-post-image" alt="Part 2: Old-timer bets in the running to be Marcos&#8217; 2nd SC justice" loading="lazy" srcset="https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/SJ-CANDIDATES-02.jpg?fit=449%2C253&amp;zoom=2 898w, https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/SJ-CANDIDATES-02.jpg?fit=449%2C253&amp;zoom=1.5 674w, https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/SJ-CANDIDATES-02.jpg?fit=449%2C253&amp;zoom=1 449w, https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/SJ-CANDIDATES-02.jpg?fit=449%2C253&amp;zoom=0.5 225w, https://www.rappler.com/tachyon/2026/10/SJ-CANDIDATES-02.jpg?fit=449%2C253&amp;zoom=0.25 112w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 449px) 100vw, 449px" />
					 	</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>


<p>On top of this, a <a href="https://www.rappler.com/philippines/261850-jbc-2020-rules-minimum-years-stint-supreme-court-philippines/">JBC 2020 rule</a> states that an SC justice must serve a minimum of 2.5 years. This means that the eldest age of a candidate should be 67.5 years old, since the mandatory retirement age for justices is 70 years old.</p>



<p>On Thursday, the JBC also published the <a href="https://www.rappler.com/philippines/chief-justice-candidates-jbc-shortlist-october-2026/">short list of chief justice nominees</a>. These are the five candidates seeking to succeed <a href="https://www.rappler.com/newsbreak/in-depth/chief-justice-alexander-gesmundo-supreme-court-stabilizing-force/">Chief Justice Alexander Gesmundo</a>:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Senior Associate Justice Marvic Leonen</li>



<li>Associate Justice Alfredo Benjamin Caguioa</li>



<li>Associate Justice Rodil Zalameda</li>



<li>Associate Justice Japar Dimaampao</li>



<li>Associate Justice Jose Midas Marquez</li>
</ul>



<p>The chief justice and associate justice posts will be Marcos’ second and third appointee to the SC, which is currently dominated by appointees of former president Rodrigo Duterte. –<strong> Rappler.com</strong></p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
